    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nAn outstanding detached four-bedroom home, No. 4 Ardgillen Lawn is a wonderfully presented property that offers generous living accommodation, excellent versatility and a superb location within this highly regarded residential development. Presented in excellent condition throughout, this attractive home is ideally suited to modern family living, with bright, well-proportioned rooms and a layout that provides both comfortable everyday living and excellent entertaining space.\nOn entering the property, the sense of space and light is immediately apparent. The accommodation is complemented by a superbly converted garage, which provides a versatile second reception room together with a separate utility area. This additional space is ideal for a family room, home office, playroom or guest accommodation, depending on the needs of the new owners. The main living accommodation is bright and generously proportioned, creating a warm and welcoming environment throughout. To the rear of the property is a separate kitchen and dining room, providing a practical and sociable space with direct access towards the rear garden. The kitchen and dining area are ideally positioned to make the most of the property's excellent outdoor space.\nOutside, the property continues to impress. The private rear garden benefits from dual side entrances and features an extensive decking area, creating an excellent setting for outdoor dining, entertaining or simply relaxing during the warmer months. To the front, the property enjoys a well-maintained garden together with ample off-street parking.\nThe home further benefits from a gas-fired central heating system, composite front door and double-glazed uPVC windows, ensuring comfort and efficiency throughout.\nArdgillen Lawn is a much sought-after cul-de-sac estate, offering a peaceful residential setting while remaining exceptionally convenient for local amenities and transport links. The property is ideally positioned between Balrothery Village and Balbriggan Town, with Balbriggan Golf Club also close by. The surrounding area offers a wide range of shops, schools, recreational facilities and transport options, making this an excellent location for families and commuters alike.\nIn summary, 4 Ardgillen Lawn is an impressive, detached family home offering generous accommodation, excellent versatility and a private rear garden, all within a desirable and convenient residential setting. Early viewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate all that this wonderful property has to offer."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 2m x 4.68m\nwith wood flooring and new composite front door, guest wc\n\nGuest WC - \nwith wood flooring, wc, whb\n\nLiving Room - 3.3m x 4.68m\nLarge bright room with feature fireplace with open fire, granite hearth, solid wood flooring, TV point, double door access to dining room\n\nKitchen - 4.53m x 3.6m\nwith tiled flooring and modern shaker kitchen with extended breakfast bar and built in hob, over and extrator, space for American style fridege freezer with built in wine rack, door to dinging room and access to rear garden.\n\nDining Room - 3.3m x 3.6m\nwith wood flooring, and access to rear garden\n\nSecond reception / office / GYM - 2.28m x 3.53m\nwith wooden flooring, TV point and door to utility room with plumbing for wahing machine and dryer.\n\nPrimary Bedroom - 3.34m x 4.68m\nLarge main bedroom with extensive built in wardrobes and TV points, door to ensuite\n\nEnsuite - 2m x 2.34m\nwith tiled flooring and half tiled walls, wc, whb & large shower unit with shower door\n\nBedroom Two - 2.24m x 4.87m\nwith wood flooring, double bedroom with built in wardrobes.\n\nBedroom Three - 3.3m x 3.6m\nwith wood flooring, double bedroom with built in wardrobes\n\nBedroom Four - 2.84m x 3.41m\nLarge single to the rear with built in wardrobes\n\n"
      },
      {
